 "notes": {
  "steep724": "All three are 7:24 tapers (3.5 in per foot, included angle 16.594 deg) with the same gauge diameters; they differ in the flange, the drive slots and the retention knob. ISO 7388-1 (forms A/AD/AF, the DIN 69871 \"SK\" holder) and ISO 7388-2 (form J, the JIS B 6339 / MAS 403 \"BT\" holder) are metric; CAT (ASME B5.50, ISO 7388-1 form U) uses an inch thread. Retention knobs (pull studs): ISO 7388-3:2016 (forms AD, AF, UD, UF, JD, JF), ASME B5.50 for CAT and JIS B 6339 for BT. Knob profiles and angles differ between machine builders, so check the machine manual before ordering.",
  "fields_steep724": [
   [
    "d1",
    "Gauge diameter d1",
    "auto"
   ],
   [
    "flange",
    "Flange diameter",
    "auto"
   ],
   [
    "thread",
    "Retention knob (pull stud) thread",
    "text"
   ]
  ],
  "morse": "Morse tapers are self-holding (about 1:20, roughly 5/8 in per foot; each size has its own ratio). Gauge diameter = diameter at the gauge line (the large end of the socket). Current standard: ISO 296:1991 (self-holding tapers for tool shanks), with DIN 228-1 the matching German standard. Morse 4 1/2 is rare and the two publishers disagree on it. Included angle = 2 atan(taper per foot / 24).",
  "jacobs": "Jacobs tapers hold drill chucks on arbors; they are not Morse tapers and the taper per foot differs between sizes (about 0.59 to 0.98 in per foot). Values as published for the Jacobs Chuck series; the drill chuck tapers of DIN 238 (B-series) are a different, metric family and are not listed here. The JT 6 and JT 33 sizes sit between JT 2 and JT 3 in diameter.",
  "hsk": "HSK hollow taper shank with flange face contact. Current standard: ISO 12164-1:2023 (shanks of types A, AB, C, CB and EB); DIN 69893-1 is the original German standard. Size = flange diameter d1 in mm (HSK-A 63 has d1 = 63 mm). HSK holders are clamped from inside by the spindle's clamping mechanism, so there is no pull stud. Only one free publisher found so far for the taper diameters; check the holder maker's drawing.",
  "r8": "R8 is a collet and toolholder taper used on knee mills (Bridgeport type), held by a 7/16-20 UNF drawbar. No international standard for R8 was found; dimensions are as published, from one source so far."
 }
